+++ b/docs/business-rules.md
@@ -69,6 +69,10 @@ ## Queue and Tickets
 
 ### Ticket
 
+- **Display code**: a per‑queue sequence `A001`, `A002`, … (prefix `A`, at least 3 digits, zero padded; beyond 999 grows: `A1000`, `A1001`).  The next code is "last valid code + 1" by insertion order, skipping any malformed legacy codes (e.g. `A‑X`).  The code is unique per `(queue_id, code)`.
+- Issuing to an inactive queue throws `InactiveQueueException`.
+- **Immutability**: Once a ticket is issued, only `status`, `called_at` and `called_by_user_id` may change.  Any attempt to modify other attributes will throw a `LogicException`.
+
 Unit of service in the queue. It is **single-use** and receives **one single call** — all data is immutable after issuance, except `called_at` and `called_by` (filled when called). Attributes:
 
 - Source queue — the ticket belongs to **one** queue (within the entity); does not record which totem it came from.
